A standard move while on portals is to #sit, and it will bring you back
to the other side without ever leaving the portal square; that way you
don't risk your life because of a set of move-away/move-back moves in
case that some critters occupie the surroundings on the other side of
the portal (or even block all possible moves away from the portal). So
in this case it is a good feature of the portal to behave so.

Now back to the observation that you reported. The code seems to operate
on each move done on the portal, whether you move onto the square, sit
on it, levitate up, or levitate down. It is supposed to work that way.

